    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "Wait, the sensor logs are pretty clear though—it shows the package wasn't bumped or dropped at all during the whole route. If we just give them credit or a replacement like you suggested, aren't we basically just paying for a customer who might have broken it themselves? Why is providing a replacement more efficient than just denying the claim based on the carrier data?",
